Well, as the subject says, I made it, finally.  It took lots of time and
careful play, but they end was semi-anticlimatic.  Now I can go on with
life!

Some observations:

1) The spell casting monsters need to have their 'zap' shortened.  When
   fighting a Lich and he hits you with frost, it takes way too long on
   a modem for all the little twinkle characters to stop.  Maybe an
   option that can be set before startup?

2)  The wizard is too agressive after he steals the amulet.  He should
	stop attacking and begin evading.  He can still send monsters to
	attack, but he should run to another room on the same level.  The
	way it is, he is too easy to kill again because he keeps coming
	back.

3)  The EndLevel was a bit tricky at first to figure out, but after I
	did it was simple to fight, kill, maim, and hack my way through the
	rooms.

4)  The oracle file should be encrypted so that it can't be read easily.
	I got some major hints from reading it, and it didn't cost me a
	thing.  You might think it was wrong to read them, but the name of the
	game is Hack, right?  Standard hack techniques to me means reading
	everything you can get your hands on!!

5)  The wand-of-wishing is great!!  I couldn't have won without it.  I
	got a quick set of gray dragon scale mail from it, a shield of
	reflection, and then used other charges to create holy water when
	the wizard cursed certain items.  It also let me get spellbooks that
	I needed in the end level.  I still had two (maybe three) wishes on
	it when I finished.


Oh well, back to real life!



